DESCRIPTION:Mark Seto directs the Brown University Orchestra in a concert 
 at The Lindemann Performing Arts Center at 7pm on Saturday\, November 21. 
 The program includes music by Florence Price\, Pablo de Sarasate\, and Pio
 tr Ilyich Tchaikovsky\, and a collaboration with student performers from C
 ommunity MusicWorks Phase II Orchestra. “Phase II” is CMW’s youth le
 adership program\, where teens build musicianship\, leadership skills\, an
 d community through chamber music\, shared meals\, and discussions. Partic
 ipants mentor younger musicians\, represent CMW in the wider community\, a
 nd organize an annual Youth Salon exploring issues they care about. World-
 renowned violinist Rachel Barton Pine is the featured soloist f\nCategory:
   Open to the Public\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/music/eve
 nt/337142-brown-university-orchestra-with-rachel-barton-pine
