BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Dance Concert 2026 — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261121T200000
DTSTAMP:20261122T065604Z
UID:555416f9b71effea3f10a78dc832@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Brown University’s Department of Theatre Arts & Performance 
 Studies present Fall Dance Concert Produced by Shura Baryshnikov Fall Danc
 e 2026 features works entirely by student makers. Created within the cours
 e Contemporary Dance Studio Project 1\, Sophia Dean ’27\, Claire Lopez 
 ’26.5\, and Rozita Papaellina ’28 share new ensemble choreographies. S
 enior Slot dance recipient Moana Marx ’27 presents a work in progress\, 
 a duet with dancers Nelah Kay and Rozita ’28 Papaellina\, as part of her
  progression towards a fully produced project for Spring Dance 2027. Novem
 ber 19 - 22 Thursday\, November 19: 8PM Friday\, November 20: 8PM Saturday
 \, November 21: 8PM Sunday\, November 22: 2PM Ashamu Dance Studio 83\nCate
 gory:  Open to the Public\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/taps
 /event/336508-fall-dance-concert-2026
LOCATION:Ashamu Dance Studio\, Ashamu Dance Studio
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/taps/event/336508-fall-dance-concert-2026
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Symphony Orchestra: The Nutcracker & Cinderella — Washi
 ngton\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261121T200000
DTSTAMP:20261122T065604Z
UID:378f632e2a53be3fb31fe6eaff51@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Be moved by two treasured fairy tales through the music of Tch
 aikovsky and Prokofiev\, conducted by Marie Jacquot in her NSO debut. Tcha
 ikovskys The Nutcracker Suite brings Clara\, the Sugar Plum Fairy\, and an
  enchanted Christmas Eve party to the concert stage\, while Prokofievs Cin
 derella Suite reimagines the timeless story with music that is playful and
  packed with clever turns. Between the ballets\, Jorge Federico Osorio cas
 ts a different kind of spell in Mozarts Piano Concerto No. 21\, famous for
  its slow\, haunting second movement. Three beloved works\, three worlds o
 f magic! There is a ticket limit of 8 tickets per person and per credit ca
 rd on this event.\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://cal
 endar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcracker-cinderella
LOCATION:Lisner Auditorium\, 730 21st Street NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcrac
 ker-cinderella
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
