DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261123T124500
DTSTAMP:20261122T065604Z
UID:8a7f1f94751c8444e4c8cdc90405@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The John Carter Brown Library is pleased to announce a year-lo
 ng exhibition titled “1776 Across the Americas: A Hemispheric History fr
 om the Collections of the John Carter Brown Library.” The exhibition is 
 now on display in the Bromsen Room at the Library and is open to the publi
 c during regular Reading Room hours. The John Carter Brown Library’s Rea
 ding Room is open Monday through Thursday from 10 a.m. to 12:45 p.m. and f
 rom 2 p.m. to 4:45 p.m.\, and Friday from 10 a.m. to 12:45 p.m. Curated by
  Beatrice and Julio Mario Santo Domingo Director and Librarian Karin Wulf 
 and JCB 2026 Postdoc Program Coordinator Kathleen Telling \, the exhibitio
 n is part of the initiative 2026 and Beyond at the JCB\nCategory:  Open to
  the Public\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/john-carter-brown-
 library/event/326697-1776-across-the-americas-a-hemispheric-history
LOCATION:94 George Street\, 94 George Street
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/john-carter-brown-library/event/326697-1776-a
 cross-the-americas-a-hemispheric-history
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Critical AI Learning Community: Casual Conversations — Providenc
 e
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261123T120000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261123T125000
DTSTAMP:20261122T065604Z
UID:a20474920eb5735505b14818e299@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Free Food\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Critical AI Learning Community. A participant-led learning com
 munity where students\, faculty\, and staff meet to explore and critique a
 rtificial intelligence technology\, and its implications for learners and 
 researchers throughout the Brown community. Learners of all levels and bac
 kgrounds are encouraged to share their experiences\, questions\, and ideas
 . This meeting will be an opportunity for casual conversations about artif
 icial intelligence. The topics for this session are: Human centered AI AI 
 and environment How are you using AI? AI skills Remember that meetings whe
 n we have casual conversations are in-person only. There will not be a Zoo
 m link. If you have not yet registered for CAILC\, p\nCategory: Free Food
 \nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/library/event/343991-critical
 -ai-learning-community-casual-conversations
LOCATION:Rockefeller Library\, Rockefeller Library
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/library/event/343991-critical-ai-learning-com
 munity-casual-conversations
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
